.TH SCRIPTS 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scripts \- unified manager for the nada.mu personal utilities ecosystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts
[\fBcommand\fR] [\fBoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscripts\fR manages the installation, updates, and removal of personal administration, workstation, and cryptographic utilities.
It supports both local development workflows and standalone remote installations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Installs scripts into the user's local path (\fB~/.local/bin\fR) or system path (\fB/usr/local/bin\fR).
.TP
.B update
Fetches updates from upstream and syncs installed utilities, reporting changed SHA-256 digests.
.TP
.B list
Lists all utilities declared in the manifest, showing their installation status and paths.
.TP
.B uninstall
Removes installed utilities, man pages, and shell completions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-scope " " \fIuser\fR|\fIsystem\fR
Target directory scope: \fBuser\fR for \fB~/.local/bin\fR (default) or \fBsystem\fR for \fB/usr/local/bin\fR (requires root).
.TP
.BR \-\-category " " \fIall\fR|\fIserver\fR|\fIdesktop\fR|\fImedia\fR
Filter which categories of scripts to install.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Run non-interactively, accepting all defaults.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help synopsis.
.SH AUTHORS
